  <h1>Predictions and offers with <em>will</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Show your present stance toward a future event: <span class="ex">I think the workshop will be busy. I’ll carry those boxes. I won’t forget the signs.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">prediction · decision · offer · promise</span>
    <span class="tag">will / ’ll / won’t + base verb</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Hear four different messages built with one modal.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Connect prediction, decision, offer, and commitment.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control form and separate offers from requests.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Respond during a fictional community event.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can make a neutral future prediction, announce a decision made now, volunteer help, make a commitment, and recognize when <span class="ex">Will you...?</span> is a request.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a prior intention, an evidence-based prediction, and a scheduled arrangement.">
    <h3>Three checks from the previous lesson</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the stated basis for each future viewpoint.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier future choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are going to invite">are going to invite</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="invited">invited</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is going to fall">is going to fall</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="falls every day">falls every day</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is coming">is coming</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="came">came</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The workshop team made this decision yesterday: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are going to invite" data-hint="The decision existed before today, so going to reports a prior intention." data-fix="They are going to invite twelve neighbors." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twelve neighbors.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The outdoor sign is loose and moving farther from the wall now: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is going to fall" data-hint="The sign’s current condition provides present evidence for the prediction." data-fix="The sign is going to fall." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The calendar confirms the technician’s appointment for exactly 9:00 Saturday: The technician <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is coming" data-hint="An exact confirmed appointment can be presented as a present-continuous arrangement." data-fix="The technician is coming at 9:00 Saturday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 9:00.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice four messages in one event-day conversation</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Saturday at Harbor Center</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Rina: I think the repair workshop will be busy today.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Lee: We need one more table. I’ll get it from the storage room.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Maya: Those boxes look heavy. I’ll carry two for you.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Rina: Thanks. I promise I won’t leave you alone at the welcome desk.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which sentence expresses a belief about the future?</li>
      <li>Which speaker decides after hearing a new need? Which speaker volunteers help?</li>
      <li>Which sentence creates a commitment between speakers?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated a prediction, immediate decision, offer, promise, invariant modal, and base verb.">
    <h3>Discovery check: identify the message</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Will meaning and form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="prediction">prediction</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="immediate decision">immediate decision</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="offer">offer</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="promise">promise</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will">will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carry">carry</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">I think the workshop will be busy</span> expresses the speaker’s present belief, so its message is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="prediction" data-hint="I think signals the speaker’s belief about a future situation." data-fix="I think the workshop will be busy is a prediction." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Lee hears a new need and says <span class="ex">I’ll get a table</span>. His choice is an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="immediate decision" data-hint="Lee decides after he hears that the group needs another table." data-fix="I’ll get a table announces an immediate decision." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Maya sees that help is useful and volunteers: <span class="ex">I’ll carry two</span> is an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="offer" data-hint="Maya volunteers to do something helpful for another person." data-fix="I’ll carry two for you is an offer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Rina adds <span class="ex">I promise</span> and commits herself: <span class="ex">I won’t leave you alone</span> is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="promise" data-hint="The explicit phrase I promise creates a commitment to the listener." data-fix="I won’t leave you alone is a promise in this context." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The modal stays the same after every subject: I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will" data-hint="Will does not change for I, she, it, or they." data-fix="I will help, she will help, and they will help all use will." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> help; she will help; they will help.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>After <span class="ex">will</span>, use the base verb: Maya will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carry" data-hint="A modal is followed directly by the base verb, without to or -s." data-fix="Maya will carry two boxes." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two boxes.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: the speaker’s present stance</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Will</span> is a modal. It does more than locate an event in future time. It shows how the speaker relates to that future event now. The speaker can present a belief, announce a choice, volunteer, or commit.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>present stance</th><th>example</th><th>speaker’s action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>belief or neutral forecast</td><td><span class="ex">I think the workshop will be busy.</span></td><td>states what seems likely</td></tr>
      <tr><td>decision announced now</td><td><span class="ex">We need tape. I’ll get some.</span></td><td>chooses in response to the situation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>willingness or offer</td><td><span class="ex">I’ll carry those boxes for you.</span></td><td>volunteers help</td></tr>
      <tr><td>commitment or promise</td><td><span class="ex">I won’t leave you alone.</span></td><td>commits to the listener</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Not every idea with <span class="ex">will</span> begins at the moment of speaking. A prediction may come from a belief you already had, and a promise may repeat an earlier commitment. The immediate-decision use is the one that specifically announces a choice made now.</p>

  <h2>Build the form: will or won’t + base verb</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>purpose</th><th>pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>positive</td><td>subject + will + base verb</td><td><span class="ex">She’ll call. They’ll help.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative</td><td>subject + won’t + base verb</td><td><span class="ex">She won’t call. They won’t wait.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>yes-or-no question</td><td>will + subject + base verb</td><td><span class="ex">Will she call?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>information question</td><td>question word + will + subject + base verb</td><td><span class="ex">When will she call?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>short answer</td><td>subject + will / won’t</td><td><span class="ex">Yes, she will. No, they won’t.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Will</span> is identical for every subject. It moves before the subject in a question and combines with <span class="ex">not</span> to make <span class="ex">won’t</span>. Do not add <span class="ex">do</span>, <span class="ex">to</span>, or third-person <span class="ex">-s</span>. Short answers keep full <span class="ex">will</span>: say <span class="ex">Yes, I will</span>, not <span class="ex">Yes, I’ll</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled invariant will, won’t, question order, information questions, short answers, and the base verb.">
    <h3>Drill 1: complete the event-day responses</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Will form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will">will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="won’t">won’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Will">Will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="When will">When will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="help">help</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="be">be</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Rina states a neutral forecast: The morning <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will" data-hint="Will stays unchanged after the singular subject morning." data-fix="The morning will be busy." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> be busy.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya makes a negative commitment: I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="won’t" data-hint="The contracted negative of will is won’t." data-fix="I won’t leave the desk unattended." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> leave the desk unattended.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Ask whether Lee is willing to carry one table: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Will" data-hint="A yes-or-no question moves Will before Lee." data-fix="Will Lee carry one table?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Lee carry one table?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Ask for the future time of the delivery: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="When will" data-hint="Begin with the information word When, then will and the subject." data-fix="When will the delivery arrive?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the delivery arrive?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>After the modal, use the base verb: The volunteers will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="help" data-hint="Will is followed directly by base-form help." data-fix="The volunteers will help at the door." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at the door.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>After <span class="ex">won’t</span>, keep the base form: Setup won’t <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="be" data-hint="Won’t is followed by base-form be, not is." data-fix="Setup won’t be difficult." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> difficult.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Answer the forecast question positively: Will the room be full? Yes, it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will" data-hint="A positive short answer uses the full modal will." data-fix="Yes, it will." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Answer the prediction question negatively: Will setup take an hour? No, it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="won’t" data-hint="A negative short answer can end with won’t." data-fix="No, it won’t." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Offer, request, decision, or prediction?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A first-person statement such as <span class="ex">I’ll carry that for you</span> can volunteer help. A question such as <span class="ex">Will you carry this box?</span> normally asks the listener to act, so it is a request, not an offer. Grammar and conversation role work together.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>context</th><th>natural response</th><th>message</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>another person needs help</td><td><span class="ex">I’ll hold the door for you.</span></td><td>offer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>you want the listener to act</td><td><span class="ex">Will you hold the door, please?</span></td><td>request</td></tr>
      <tr><td>a new problem appears</td><td><span class="ex">We need tape. I’ll get some.</span></td><td>immediate decision</td></tr>
      <tr><td>you state what seems likely</td><td><span class="ex">I think more people will arrive soon.</span></td><td>prediction</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Accept an offer with <span class="ex">Thanks</span> or <span class="ex">Yes, please</span>. Decline with <span class="ex">No, thanks</span>. <span class="ex">Yes, I will</span> answers a question about your own future action or willingness; it is not the normal answer to <span class="ex">I’ll help you</span>.</p>

  <h3>Compare <em>will</em> and <em>going to</em> without a rigid rule</h3>
  <p><span class="ex">Going to</span> commonly foregrounds a prior intention or a result supported by present evidence. <span class="ex">Will</span> commonly presents a decision announced now or a neutral belief and forecast. This is a useful A2 contrast, not a law that makes every other choice impossible.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <p><span class="ex">We decided yesterday. We’re going to print twenty signs.</span> The speaker foregrounds the prior plan.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">We need one more sign. I’ll print it now.</span> The speaker announces a response to the new need.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">That loose sign is going to fall.</span> The current physical evidence points toward the result.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">I think the event will become popular.</span> The speaker gives a neutral belief about the future.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You used the conversational context to identify an offer, request, immediate decision, neutral prediction, prior intention, and evidence prediction.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the message that fits</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Future message choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I’ll carry it for you">I’ll carry it for you</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Will you carry it, please">Will you carry it, please</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I’ll get some">I’ll get some</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will become popular">will become popular</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are going to print">are going to print</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is going to fall">is going to fall</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya sees Rina struggling with a heavy box and volunteers: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I’ll carry it for you" data-hint="A first-person will statement can volunteer the speaker’s help." data-fix="I’ll carry it for you is an offer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Rina needs Lee to move a box and asks him directly: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Will you carry it, please" data-hint="Will you plus an action asks the listener to do something." data-fix="Will you carry it, please? is a request." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>?”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The team discovers that there is no tape, and Lee decides at that moment: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I’ll get some" data-hint="Lee’s choice responds immediately to the newly stated problem." data-fix="I’ll get some announces Lee’s immediate decision." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Rina gives a belief, not a visible-result prediction: I think the workshop <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will become popular" data-hint="I think frames a neutral belief about the event’s future." data-fix="I think the workshop will become popular." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The notes prove that the team decided yesterday: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are going to print" data-hint="The earlier decision provides the basis for a going-to intention." data-fix="They are going to print twenty signs." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twenty signs.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The sign is visibly loose and moving away from the wall: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is going to fall" data-hint="The present physical evidence supports going to as the foregrounded prediction." data-fix="The sign is going to fall." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: weak <em>’ll</em>, clear <em>won’t</em>, and sentence stress</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In relaxed U.S. English, <span class="ex">will</span> usually contracts after a pronoun: <span class="ex">I’ll, you’ll, he’ll, she’ll, it’ll, we’ll, they’ll</span>. The contraction can sound like a very short <span class="ex">l</span> attached to the pronoun. Stress the useful new information: <span class="ex">I’ll <strong>GET</strong> the tape. She’ll <strong>CALL</strong> at <strong>FIVE</strong>.</span></p>
  <p><span class="ex">Won’t</span> has the long vowel heard in U.S. <span class="ex">go</span>: /woʊnt/. It does not sound like <span class="ex">want</span>. Use stronger stress when the negative commitment or contrast matters: <span class="ex">I <strong>WON’T</strong> forget.</span> Full <span class="ex">will</span> can also carry contrast: <span class="ex">I <strong>WILL</strong> call, even if I’m busy.</span></p>

  <h3>Place probability words where listeners expect them</h3>
  <p>In an affirmative prediction, <span class="ex">probably</span> normally follows <span class="ex">will</span>: <span class="ex">It will probably be busy.</span> In a negative prediction, it normally comes before <span class="ex">won’t</span>: <span class="ex">It probably won’t take long.</span> <span class="ex">Maybe</span> naturally opens the complete clause: <span class="ex">Maybe more people will come.</span></p>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read prediction, immediate decision, offer, promise, request, and evidence-based future listening check">
    <h2>Listen: what is the speaker doing?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each fictional line once naturally and once more slowly. Listen for the conversational role, not only the word <span class="ex">will</span>. Open the script only after checking.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard a neutral prediction, immediate decision, offer, promise, request, and evidence-based going-to prediction.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a neutral prediction" data-hint="I think frames the speaker’s belief about attendance." data-fix="I think more people will arrive soon is a neutral prediction."><p class="quiz-question">1. What is the speaker doing in Clip 1?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a neutral prediction">a neutral prediction</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="making a request">making a request</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="reporting a past result">reporting a past result</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="deciding to get tape now" data-hint="The missing tape is a new problem, and the speaker responds immediately." data-fix="We need tape. I’ll get some announces a decision made now."><p class="quiz-question">2. What decision occurs in Clip 2?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="deciding to get tape now">deciding to get tape now</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="repeating yesterday’s tape plan">repeating yesterday’s tape plan</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="refusing to get tape">refusing to get tape</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the speaker offers to carry two boxes" data-hint="The first-person I’ll statement volunteers useful help." data-fix="Those boxes look heavy. I’ll carry two for you is an offer."><p class="quiz-question">3. What happens in Clip 3?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker offers to carry two boxes">the speaker offers to carry two boxes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker requests two boxes">the speaker requests two boxes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker predicts two boxes">the speaker predicts two boxes</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the speaker commits not to leave" data-hint="I promise plus won’t creates a negative commitment." data-fix="I promise I won’t leave you alone commits the speaker not to leave."><p class="quiz-question">4. What does Clip 4 commit the speaker to?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker commits not to leave">the speaker commits not to leave</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the listener must leave">the listener must leave</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker already left">the speaker already left</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the listener is asked to hold the door" data-hint="Will you plus the action directs a polite request to the listener." data-fix="Will you hold the door, please? asks the listener to act."><p class="quiz-question">5. Who is expected to act after Clip 5?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the listener is asked to hold the door">the listener is asked to hold the door</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker offers to hold the door">the speaker offers to hold the door</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="nobody needs to hold the door">nobody needs to hold the door</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the sign is loose and moving" data-hint="The present physical condition of the sign supports the going-to prediction." data-fix="The sign is loose and moving, so it is going to fall."><p class="quiz-question">6. What evidence supports Clip 6?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the sign is loose and moving">the sign is loose and moving</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="someone decided to drop the sign">someone decided to drop the sign</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the sign fell last week">the sign fell last week</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="thinking-card">
      <summary>Open the teacher script after checking</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">I think more people will arrive soon.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">We need tape. I’ll get some.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Those boxes look heavy. I’ll carry two for you.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">I promise I won’t leave you alone at the desk.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Will you hold the door, please?</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">That sign is loose and moving. It’s going to fall.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read the event-day group chat</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Center, 8:45 a.m.</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Rina: I think about twenty people will come this morning.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Lee: We only have ten chairs here.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Maya: I’ll bring five more from Room B.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Rina: Thanks. Will you ask Omar to bring the other five, please?</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Lee: I’ll ask him now. I promise I won’t forget.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You followed the forecast, offer, request, immediate decision, and promise in the group chat.">
    <h3>Read, then choose the exact evidence</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="about twenty people will come" data-hint="Rina’s first message states her belief about attendance." data-fix="Rina predicts that about twenty people will come."><p class="quiz-question">1. What does Rina predict?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="about twenty people will come">about twenty people will come</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="only ten people will come">only ten people will come</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the event will move to Room B">the event will move to Room B</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya offers to bring five chairs" data-hint="Maya volunteers with a first-person I’ll statement after Lee identifies a need." data-fix="Maya says I’ll bring five more, so she offers to help."><p class="quiz-question">2. What help does Maya volunteer?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya offers to bring five chairs">Maya offers to bring five chairs</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya asks Omar for ten chairs">Maya asks Omar for ten chairs</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya promises to count the visitors">Maya promises to count the visitors</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Rina asks Lee to speak to Omar" data-hint="Will you ask Omar directs the requested action to Lee." data-fix="Rina asks Lee to speak to Omar about the other chairs."><p class="quiz-question">3. What is the request in the chat?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina asks Lee to speak to Omar">Rina asks Lee to speak to Omar</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Lee asks Rina to move rooms">Lee asks Rina to move rooms</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar asks Maya to count chairs">Omar asks Maya to count chairs</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the offer and the request</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i’ll carry two boxes for you" data-hint="Begin with first-person I’ll, then the base verb carry, object, and for-you phrase." data-fix="I’ll carry two boxes for you." data-success-message="Correct. The first-person will statement volunteers the speaker’s help.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the offer</h3><p class="tile-target">Maya sees that Rina needs help.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="two">two</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="carry">carry</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i’ll">I’ll</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="for">for</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="boxes">boxes</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="will you hold the door please" data-hint="Move Will before you, then add the base verb, object, and please." data-fix="Will you hold the door, please?" data-success-message="Correct. Will you plus the action asks the listener to hold the door.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the request</h3><p class="tile-target">Rina needs Lee to act.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="door">door</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="please">please</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="will">Will</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="hold">hold</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three high-value errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="wills" data-hint="Will is invariant, so it does not take third-person -s after she." data-fix="She will call the volunteers at nine." data-why="The modal will has one form for every subject, so wills must become will." data-success-message="Correct. You restored the invariant modal form will.">
    <h3>Drill 5: one modal form for every subject</h3><p>The update says, “She wills call the volunteers at nine.” Tap the word to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="wills">wills</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="call">call</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="volunteers">the volunteers</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="nine">at nine.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="A modal is followed directly by the base verb, with no to." data-fix="I’ll carry those boxes for you." data-why="Will is followed directly by carry, so to must be removed." data-success-message="Correct. You placed the base verb directly after will.">
    <h3>Drill 6: no <em>to</em> after will</h3><p>Maya offers, “I’ll to carry those boxes for you.” Tap the word to remove.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i’ll">I’ll</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="carry">carry</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="boxes">those boxes</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">for you.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="offer-label" data-hint="Will you asks the listener to act; an offer volunteers the speaker’s action with I’ll." data-fix="Request: Will you hold the door, please? Offer: I’ll hold the door for you." data-why="The subject identifies who is expected to act. You makes it a request to the listener; I makes it the speaker’s offer." data-success-message="Correct. You separated a request to the listener from an offer by the speaker.">
    <h3>Drill 7: who is expected to act?</h3><p>The note labels “Will you hold the door, please?” as an offer. Tap the label to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="offer-label">offer</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="will">Will</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hold">hold the door, please?</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transform: preserve the conversational role</h3>
    <p>Say every response before revealing it.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> You believe the workshop will be busy. Add a probability word.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The workshop will probably be busy.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> There is no tape. Decide now to get some.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’ll get some.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> Rina’s box is heavy. Volunteer to carry it.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’ll carry it for you.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> You need Lee to close the window. Make a polite request with will.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Will you close the window, please?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Commit not to forget the signs.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I promise I won’t forget the signs.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> The team decided yesterday to print signs. Report the prior intention.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They’re going to print the signs.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it: respond during a fictional event</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real work, study, home, location, schedule, travel, family, relationships, finances, devices, health, promises, or future plans. Use the fictional workshop, invent a public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Forecast the event:</b> Make three neutral predictions about fictional attendance, timing, and results. Use <span class="ex">I think</span>, <span class="ex">probably</span>, and <span class="ex">maybe</span> accurately.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Respond to new needs:</b> Your teacher announces three fictional problems during the event. Make an immediate decision for one and offer help for two.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask and respond:</b> Make two requests with <span class="ex">Will you...?</span>. Accept or decline two offers naturally with <span class="ex">Thanks</span>, <span class="ex">Yes, please</span>, or <span class="ex">No, thanks</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a 45–60 second event-day response.</b> Include one neutral prediction, one immediate decision, two offers, one request, one positive or negative commitment, and one contrast with a prior <span class="ex">going to</span> plan. Finish by explaining who acts in your request and your offer.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled modal stance, form, prediction, immediate decision, offer, request, promise, probability words, and the going-to boundary.">
    <h3>Eight decisions from a library open house</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="will probably attract" data-hint="The coordinator gives a neutral belief, and probably follows will." data-fix="I think the open house will probably attract new visitors."><p class="quiz-question">1. The coordinator gives a neutral forecast: I think the open house ___ new visitors.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="will probably attract">will probably attract</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="will attract probably">will attract probably</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="probably will attracting">probably will attracting</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I’ll print one" data-hint="The speaker responds immediately after discovering the missing sign." data-fix="We need one more sign. I’ll print one."><p class="quiz-question">2. The team has just discovered a missing sign. Which reply announces a decision made now?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’ll print one">I’ll print one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I printed one yesterday">I printed one yesterday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I print one every week">I print one every week</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I’ll carry that for you" data-hint="The first-person statement volunteers the speaker’s action for another person." data-fix="I’ll carry that for you is an offer."><p class="quiz-question">3. A visitor is struggling with a heavy display. Which sentence offers help?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’ll carry that for you">I’ll carry that for you</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Will you carry that?">Will you carry that?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You carried that yesterday">You carried that yesterday</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Will you open the side door, please?" data-hint="Will you directs the requested action to the listener." data-fix="Will you open the side door, please? is a request."><p class="quiz-question">4. The coordinator needs a volunteer to act. Which sentence makes the request?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Will you open the side door, please?">Will you open the side door, please?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I’ll open the side door for you.">I’ll open the side door for you.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The side door opened yesterday.">The side door opened yesterday.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I promise I won’t share the draft" data-hint="The explicit phrase I promise turns the negative will statement into a commitment." data-fix="I promise I won’t share the draft is a negative promise."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence clearly creates a commitment?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I promise I won’t share the draft">I promise I won’t share the draft</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maybe the draft will change">Maybe the draft will change</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Will the draft be ready?">Will the draft be ready?</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="will arrive" data-hint="Will takes the base verb arrive, with no to or -s." data-fix="She will arrive at ten."><p class="quiz-question">6. Complete the modal form: She ___ at ten.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="will arrive">will arrive</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="will arrives">will arrives</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="will to arrive">will to arrive</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is going to fall" data-hint="The shelf is visibly leaning now, so the present evidence is foregrounded." data-fix="That shelf is going to fall."><p class="quiz-question">7. A shelf is visibly leaning farther forward right now: It ___.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is going to fall">is going to fall</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="falls every Monday">falls every Monday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fell tomorrow">fell tomorrow</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maybe more visitors will come" data-hint="Maybe naturally opens the complete clause, followed by subject, will, and base verb." data-fix="Maybe more visitors will come after lunch."><p class="quiz-question">8. Which probability sentence has natural word order?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maybe more visitors will come">Maybe more visitors will come</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="More visitors maybe will coming">More visitors maybe will coming</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Will maybe come more visitors">Will maybe come more visitors</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect and plan the next use</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Can you explain the speaker’s stance?</h3>
    <p>Explain the difference among <span class="ex">I think it will be busy</span>, <span class="ex">I’ll get another chair</span>, <span class="ex">I’ll carry that for you</span>, and <span class="ex">I promise I won’t forget</span>. Then explain why <span class="ex">Will you carry it?</span> is normally a request.</p>
    <p>Choose your next use: repeat the event response with fewer notes, create three offer-and-request pairs, or complete the retrieval below tomorrow.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the stance, form, conversation role, probability word, or future contrast that still feels slow.</p>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day prediction, offer, request, and future-choice retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a neutral prediction, an offer, and a request from their conversational contexts.">
      <h3>Choose from memory before looking back</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day will choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will probably be">will probably be</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="probably will being">probably will being</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I’ll hold it for you">I’ll hold it for you</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="You will hold it for me">You will hold it for me</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Will you close it, please">Will you close it, please</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I’ll close it for you">I’ll close it for you</button></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The speaker gives a neutral forecast with natural probability-word order: The afternoon <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will probably be" data-hint="In an affirmative prediction, probably normally follows will and precedes the base verb be." data-fix="The afternoon will probably be busy." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> busy.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Rina’s display is heavy, and Maya volunteers her own help: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="I’ll hold it for you" data-hint="The first-person I’ll statement volunteers the speaker’s action." data-fix="I’ll hold it for you is an offer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.”</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Rina needs Lee to close the window and asks him to act: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Will you close it, please" data-hint="Will you plus the action directs a request to the listener." data-fix="Will you close it, please? is a request." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>?”</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="Will is followed directly by the base verb, without to." data-fix="I’ll carry the display for you." data-why="The modal will connects directly to base-form carry, so to must be removed." data-success-message="Correct. You restored will plus the base verb.">
      <h3>Repair one high-risk offer</h3><p>Maya says, “I’ll to carry the display for you.” Tap the word to remove.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i’ll">I’ll</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="carry">carry</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="display">the display</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">for you.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Thirty-second retrieval</h3>
      <p>Without looking back, give one neutral prediction, one immediate decision, one offer, one request, one promise, and one prior intention with <span class="ex">going to</span>.</p>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
      <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I think it will be busy. We need tape, so I’ll get some. I’ll carry that for you. Will you hold the door, please? I promise I won’t forget. We’re going to print signs because we decided yesterday.</strong></p>
